-- ClassLess -- one ability per fight, drawn at random from the creature's own tome pool.
--
-- GENERATED by tools/classless-web/npc_showcast.py -- regenerate, do not hand-edit.
--
--   id 900      SMART_EVENT_AGGRO     -> RANDOM_PHASE, up to 6 phases, target SELF
--   id 901-906  SMART_EVENT_HEALTH_PCT -> CAST, one per phase, NOT_REPEATABLE, health 5-95%
--
-- The phase is rolled fresh at every aggro, so the same creature shows a different book on
-- the next pull. IsInPhase is false while the phase is 0, so nothing happens before the
-- first fight; the health band is only read for an event in phase, so it starts answering
-- at aggro and not at spawn; SmartScript::OnReset clears runOnce, so evade and respawn
-- re-arm the one attempt.
--
-- The band is health and not a timer because the shown ability is now the one the corpse
-- may give up (Server.lua). A 4-12 second timer is a bet that the fight lasts that long,
-- and a levelling mob dies in two; every creature fought down rather than one-shot passes
-- through the band whatever its health pool.
--
-- Auras are deliberately absent. An earlier version wore one icon aura per line it dropped;
-- under the group rule a creature answers for a median of three groups and the buff row
-- became a wall of pictures. The performance is the whole of the tell now.
--
-- Re-runnable in both directions: the DELETE owns the whole id band and the AIName grant is
-- handed back from state, not from a list, so nothing here is a one-way door.

-- The WHOLE band, with no entry filter. Scoping the delete to the creatures getting a row
-- THIS time leaves rows behind on every creature that has since stopped qualifying.
DELETE FROM `smart_scripts` WHERE `source_type` = 0 AND `id` BETWEEN 900 AND 909;

-- Creatures with no AI at all. Guarded on AIName and ScriptName so this can
-- never take a scripted creature's behaviour away, and asserted for EVERY
-- scripted carrier rather than only the ones empty right now: naming only the
-- latter makes the statement vanish once the file has been applied, and then a
-- realm built from zero gets smart_scripts rows on creatures that never became
-- SmartAI.
